   "text": "PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR 7.1S 68.9E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 8.7S 68.6E, APPROXIMATELY 244 NM WEST- SOUTHWEST OF DIEGO GARCIA. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED (EIR) SATELLITE IMAGERY DEPICTS DEEP CONVECTION FLARING OVER A COMPACT LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC). A 251556Z ASCAT-B PASS SHOWS A DEFINED SURFACE CIRCULATION WITH 20-25 KT WINDS TO THE SOUTHWEST. ENVIRONMENTAL ANALYSIS REVEALS A MODERATELY FAVORABLE ENVIRONMENT FOR DEVELOPMENT WITH MODERATE VERTICAL WIND SHEAR (VWS) OF 15-20 KNOTS, MODERATE POLEWARD UPPER-LEVEL OUTFLOW, AND WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES (SST) OF 28-29 C. GLOBAL MODELS ARE IN GOOD AGREEMENT THAT INVEST 97S WILL CONTINUE TO SLOWLY CONSOLIDATE WHILE MAINTAINING A QUASI-STATIONARY MOTION OVER THE NEXT 24 HOURS. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 23 TO 28 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1008 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS IS MEDIUM.",
