   "text": "PREVIOUSLY LOCATED NEAR 8.9S 78.6E IS NOW LOCATED NEAR 11.0S 78.0E, APPROXIMATELY 395 NM SOUTHEAST OF DIEGO GARCIA. ANIMATED ENHANCED INFRARED (EIR) SATELLITE IMAGERY DEPICTS A PARTIALLY EXPOSED LOW-LEVEL CIRCULATION CENTER (LLCC), WITH RENEWED CONVECTIVE ACTIVITY NEAR THE CENTER. A 250342Z ASCAT-C PASS REVEALED A DEFINED SURFACE CIRCULATION WITH NEAR GALE- FORCE WINDS IN THE NORTHWEST QUADRANT. UPPER-LEVEL ANALYSIS INDICATES MODEST POLEWARD OUTFLOW ALOFT, MODERATE (15-20 KTS) VERTICAL WIND SHEAR (VWS), AND WARM SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES (SST) OF 28-29 C. GLOBAL MODELS DEPICT INCREASING VWS, WHICH WILL LIMIT FURTHER DEVELOPMENT AND BEGIN TO INDUCE WEAKENING OVER THE NEXT 24-48 HOURS AS THE SYSTEM MOVES GENERALLY POLEWARD. MAXIMUM SUSTAINED SURFACE WINDS ARE ESTIMATED AT 27 TO 32 KNOTS. MINIMUM SEA LEVEL PRESSURE IS ESTIMATED TO BE NEAR 1009 MB. THE POTENTIAL FOR THE DEVELOPMENT OF A SIGNIFICANT TROPICAL CYCLONE WITHIN THE NEXT 24 HOURS IS LOW.",
